  "figures": [
    {
      "caption": "A frozen JEPA model chooses actions from RGB history and an RGB goal by exhaustive one- or three-step latent-distance search. The three-step cost sums all predicted stage distances. Random and fixed-cycle policies use the same 128 starts and goals; the state oracle is a privileged reference with physical-position access. Goals are 6\u201312 cardinal actions away. Bars show exact goal hits before native death or the 24-action limit; whiskers are Wilson 95% intervals across starts, separately for each checkpoint. Model-seed results are not pooled into a larger binomial sample. This is empty-arena navigation, not strategic planning.",
